# Build output.
target/
__pycache__/
.claude

# The box's own compose overlay: which proxy network to join, which port to
# publish. Belongs to the machine, not to the project, and reset --hard leaves
# it alone the same way it leaves .env alone.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Credentials. The deployment reads GH_TOKEN, OLLAMA_API_KEY and friends from
# here, so this file is the one thing in the tree that must never be committed.
# It was untracked and unignored for a while, which is one `git add .` away from
# being in the history for good.
.env
# Snapshots. Every rendering decision in here was checked by dumping a frame to
# PNG (see map/scripts/ansi2png.py); none of those frames are source.
*.png
# -- except the ones in assets/, which are. portraits.py bakes them into
# portfolio/src/portraits.rs, and without the originals that file cannot be
# regenerated at any other size.
!assets/*.png

# The basemap archive, kept at the top level so it is mounted rather than
# symlinked into map/data. 1.7 GB: this must never reach a commit, and it is
# listed before anything else here for that reason.
map-data/

# Basemaps and everything derived from them: ~110 MB here, plus a symlink to a
# 1.6 GB PMTiles archive. All of it is rebuildable from the scripts in
# map/scripts, and none of it is authored.
#
# The tour sheet is the exception. It lives under data/ because that is where
# the loader looks, but it is hand-written content — the experience section's
# entire text — and not data at all.
map/data/*
!map/data/places.txt

# Somebody else's repository, cloned in as reference for `moonin`: 37 MB with
# its own .git, its own README and its own LICENSE. Committing it would either
# vendor another project's history into this one or leave a gitlink nothing here
# can resolve. `moonin/refs/*.png` is covered by the rule above.
moonin/ian-xiaohei-illustrations-en/
